## Build output
bin/
obj/
publish/

## Test artefacts
TestResults/
*.trx
*.dmp
*.hangdump

## Screenshots produced by Tools/RenderShots. Its default output directory is
## "shots" (CWD-relative), which is what CI writes into.
shots/
screenshots/
*.png

## ...except the icon PNGs, which are source assets. The .ico is generated from
## the same vector mark by Tools/MakeIcon and is committed alongside them so a
## clean clone builds with no image tooling. The PNGs are the reviewable form of
## each frame. Negation has to come after the rule above, and needs the
## directory anchor or git will not descend into Assets to find them.
!Assets/*.png

## Installer output. The .wxs source is committed; everything WiX produces from
## it is not. That includes the 36MB MSI plus the .cab and .wixpdb it leaves
## behind as build intermediates.
installer/*.msi
installer/*.wixpdb
installer/*.cab
installer/*.zip
installer/obj/
installer/bin/

## MSIX / Microsoft Store build output.
## AppXManifest.xml IS committed - it is source. AppxAssets\ IS committed - the
## artwork is generated but versioned. Everything else below is rebuilt by
## build-msix.ps1 and must not be committed.
installer/*.msix
installer/*.msix.cat
installer/AppXManifest.build.xml
msix-stage/

## Undo the blanket *.png rule for the Store artwork only. A broad *.png rule
## exists elsewhere in this file, and without this the AppxAssets the manifest
## references would be missing from a fresh clone - which fails makeappx
## validation at pack time.
!installer/AppxAssets/*.png

## Editor / OS noise
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

## Secrets — none are expected in this repo, but keep it that way
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
.env
.env.local
appsettings.Development.json
